<title>USA: FORECAST- Rising distillates focus of API report.</title>
<headline>FORECAST- Rising distillates focus of API report.</headline>
<byline>Harry Milling</byline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The American Petroleum Institute (API) is expected to show another bearishly large rise in distillate stocks in its inventory data Tuesday, though traders anticipate the rate of build may trail off.</p>
<p>&quot;I just don't think refineries can sustain their record output, and exports have fallen,&quot; said William Brown, president of W.H. Brown &amp; Co, a trading firm.</p>
<p>A survey done by Reuters forecasts distillate stocks building 2.5 million barrels for the week ended November 1 compared with a build of 3.6 million in the week of October 25.</p>
</text>
